body:
I found another somewhat related issue in the context of Controller unit testing.

I'm unable to mock the Request object to be a Basic authorization. I'm doing this:

``` php
$this->configRequest([
    'headers' => [
        'Authorization' => 'Basic ' . base64_encode($username . ':' . $password)
    ],
    'environment' => [
        'PHP_AUTH_USER' => $username,
        'PHP_AUTH_PW' => $password
    ]
]);
```

and inside the `IntegrationTestCase::_buildRequest()` method the following logic prevents me from setting mocked environment variables in the Request object that gets passed to the dispatcher:

``` php
$env = [];
if (isset($this->_request['headers'])) {
    foreach ($this->_request['headers'] as $k => $v) {
        $env['HTTP_' . str_replace('-', '_', strtoupper($k))] = $v;
    }
    unset($this->_request['headers']);
}
$env['REQUEST_METHOD'] = $method;
$props['environment'] = $env;
```
